From: Onur Bingol <obingol@anaconda.com>
Subject: [PATCH] win32: select bundled DLL suffix from interpreter ABI (PR #177) + GLUT/GLE fallback

Select the bundled DLLS suffix from sysconfig.get_platform() —
win32 -> 32, win-amd64 -> 64, win-arm64 -> arm64 — instead of pointer
width via platform.architecture(). ARM64 and AMD64 are both 64-bit,
so the old code requested the AMD64 gle64/freeglut64 builds on
native ARM64 Python, which cannot be loaded. Sysconfig describes the
interpreter build, so AMD64 Python running under emulation still
selects '64'. Unknown platforms stay distinct so the loader falls
back to no optional DLL rather than trying an x86 binary.

Also adds a bare 'gle' fallback so a user-provided gle.dll loads
when no bundled DLL is installed (win-64 unvendored DLLS/) and
makes GLUT/GLE try the system freeglut first (conda freeglut run
dep). Needed for the win-arm64 native GLE build
(glearm64.vc14.dll) installed by bld.bat into OpenGL/DLLS/.

Status: backport of mcfletch/pyopengl#177 (unmerged upstream).
--- a/OpenGL/platform/win32.py
+++ b/OpenGL/platform/win32.py
@@ -1,6 +1,6 @@
 """Windows-specific platform features"""
 import ctypes
-import platform
+import sysconfig
 from OpenGL.platform import ctypesloader, baseplatform
 import sys
 
@@ -14,7 +14,15 @@
     vc = 'vc9'
 
 def _size():
-    return platform.architecture()[0].strip( 'bits' )
+    # Anaconda: select the bundled DLL suffix from the interpreter ABI,
+    # not the pointer width (mcfletch/pyopengl#177). ARM64 and AMD64 are
+    # both 64-bit, so pointer width would wrongly request AMD64 DLLs on
+    # native win-arm64 Python. Sysconfig describes the interpreter build.
+    # This also fixes AMD64 Python running under emulation: it still
+    # selects '64'. Unknown platforms stay distinct (loader falls back
+    # to no optional DLL rather than trying an x86 binary).
+    target = sysconfig.get_platform()
+    return {'win32': '32', 'win-amd64': '64', 'win-arm64': 'arm64'}.get(target, target)
 size = _size()
 
 class Win32Platform( baseplatform.BasePlatform ):
@@ -39,6 +47,8 @@
             return None
     @baseplatform.lazy_property
     def GLUT( self ):
+        # Anaconda: try the system freeglut first (conda freeglut run dep),
+        # then the bundled 'arm64'-suffixed name on win-arm64.
         for possible in ('freeglut%s.%s'%(size,vc,), 'glut%s.%s'%(size,vc,)):
             # Prefer FreeGLUT if the user has installed it, fallback to the included 
             # GLUT if it is installed
@@ -51,7 +61,12 @@
         return None
     @baseplatform.lazy_property
     def GLE( self ):
-        for libName in ('gle%s.%s'%(size,vc,), 'opengle%s.%s'%(size,vc,)):
+        # Anaconda: on win-arm64 _size() is 'arm64', so this tries
+        # glearm64.vc14.dll -- built natively from GLE 3.1.0 by build.sh
+        # and installed into OpenGL/DLLS/. On win-64 it tries the
+        # standard gle64.vc14.dll names. Falls back to bare 'gle' for a
+        # user-provided DLL.
+        for libName in ('gle%s.%s'%(size,vc,), 'opengle%s.%s'%(size,vc,), 'gle'):
             try:
                 GLE = ctypesloader.loadLibrary( ctypes.cdll, libName )
                 GLE.FunctionType = ctypes.CFUNCTYPE
